# Optical-flow fallback for GPS-denied flight - quadcopter, ArduCopter 4.7.1.
#
# Apply AFTER gps_denied_extnav.param (this file only adds source set 2 and the
# flow sensor). Source set 1 = VIO (ExternalNav); source set 2 = optical flow for
# horizontal velocity + barometer for height, with the downward rangefinder the EKF
# needs to scale flow. Reboot the FC after applying (FLOW_TYPE is read at boot).
#
# Switching between the sets, any of:
#   * an RC switch: RCx_OPTION 90 "EKF Source Set" - low = set 1, middle = set 2,
#     high = set 3 (libraries/RC_Channel/RC_Channel.h:258, RC_Channel.cpp:1692).
#     Not set here: pick a free channel on the transmitter and set RCx_OPTION 90
#     yourself (e.g. RC8_OPTION 90) - writing one blindly could clobber an existing
#     aux function.
#   * MAVLink MAV_CMD_SET_EKF_SOURCE_SET (42007), param1 = 1..3
#     (GCS_Common.cpp handle_command_set_ekf_source_set): drone_sdk._set_ekf_source_set(n),
#     or VioBridge(fallback_source_set=2) to switch automatically when the VIO is lost.
#
# Sources: [SRC] libraries/AP_NavEKF/AP_NavEKF_Source.cpp; [FLOW]
# libraries/AP_OpticalFlow/AP_OpticalFlow.cpp; [WIKI-SRC]
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/common-ekf-sources.html (whose worked example is
# exactly this: SRC1 ExternalNav, SRC2 POSXY 0 / VELXY 5).
# Comments must start a line (AP_Param::parse_param_line).

# FLOW_TYPE: 0:None, 1:PX4Flow, 2:Pixart, 3:Bebop, 4:CXOF, 5:MAVLink, 6:DroneCAN,
# 7:MSP, 8:UPFLOW, 10:SITL [FLOW :30]. REVIEW BEFORE APPLYING: the quadcopter has no
# dedicated flow sensor today. 5 = MAVLink OPTICAL_FLOW from the companion (e.g.
# computed from the downward D430's IR stream - NOT implemented in this repo yet).
# If you fit a sensor, use its type instead. With no flow data, set 2 has no
# horizontal source and switching to it gives ALT_HOLD-grade flight only.
FLOW_TYPE 5

# EK3_SRC2_POSXY: 0 = None - flow gives velocity only, no position [SRC :66, WIKI-SRC]
EK3_SRC2_POSXY 0
# EK3_SRC2_VELXY: 5 = OpticalFlow [SRC :73, WIKI-SRC]
EK3_SRC2_VELXY 5
# EK3_SRC2_POSZ: 1 = Baro [SRC :80] - the same as set 1, so a switch never resets
# height. (2 = RangeFinder is height above whatever is underneath, which steps at
# every obstacle; the EKF already uses the rangefinder for flow's terrain height.)
EK3_SRC2_POSZ 1
# EK3_SRC2_VELZ: 0 = None - flow has no vertical velocity [SRC :87]
EK3_SRC2_VELZ 0
# EK3_SRC2_YAW: 1 = Compass [SRC :94]. ExternalNav yaw is gone when the VIO is,
# which is why this set exists. Expect a heading reset to the compass at the switch;
# keep the compass calibrated (indoors near steel it can be badly off).
EK3_SRC2_YAW 1

# EK3_SRC_OPTIONS bit 1 = AlignExtNavPosWhenUsingOptFlow [SRC :139]: while flying on
# flow, the inactive ExternalNav position is kept aligned to the EKF's
# (AP_NavEKF_Source::align_inactive_sources), so switching back to the VIO (set 1)
# does not jump. Bit 0 (FuseAllVelocities) stays off: VIO and flow velocities would
# both be fused, and when the VIO goes bad that is exactly what must stop.
EK3_SRC_OPTIONS 2

# Not set here, check by hand:
# * A downward rangefinder (RNGFNDn_ORIENT 25) must be configured - the quadcopter has
#   two. FLOW_FXSCALER / FLOW_FYSCALER / FLOW_ORIENT_YAW / FLOW_POS_* are per-sensor
#   calibration: follow the flow-sensor setup page after fitting one.
# * EK3_FLOW_DELAY (default 10 ms) is sensor-specific.
